{
 "id": "mobility-foundation",
 "name": "Mobility Foundation",
 "family": "Mobility",
 "difficulty": "Beginner",
 "durationWeeks": 4,
 "frequencyPerWeek": 5,
 "environment": "Home — a floor, a wall and a doorway",
 "description": "Four weeks, five short sessions a week, on the floor of whatever room you are in. This is not a workout and it is not meant to feel like one — it is the practice that runs alongside your training and keeps your hips, shoulders, ankles and spine moving the way they are supposed to. Each session opens with breathing or gentle whole-body movement, works the joints of the day, and finishes with holds. The positions never get harder. What changes is how long you stay in them: twenty seconds in week one, fifty in week four. Learning to be comfortable in a position is the whole skill, and it is the one that carries into every other program you run.",
 "goals": [
  "Build a mobility practice you actually keep",
  "Learn foundational positions and how to breathe in them",
  "Move every major region across the week — hips, shoulders, spine, ankles",
  "Hold a stretch for fifty seconds without fighting it",
  "Arrive ready for the deeper positions of Mobility Intermediate"
